id: 3
hanzi: 组合
pinyin: zǔ hé
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to combine; assemble; composite; combination
  es: combinar; asociar; integrar; combinación; conjunto

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to unite or bring together distinct components, persons, or groups into a coherent whole | unir o enlazar elementos, personas o piezas diversas para formar un todo estructurado | 自由组合成学习小组 (combine freely into study groups)
  2 | Noun | Standard | a combination, composite arrangement, or musical group | conjunto estructurado de partes o agrupación artística | 经典的沙发家具组合 (a classic sofa furniture combination set)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 这套组合音响设备不仅音质清澈饱满，还支持多种无线传输协议，深受年轻音乐爱好者的青睐。 | Zhè tào zǔhé yīnxiǎng shèbèi bùjǐn yīnzhì qīngchè bǎomǎn, hái zhīchí duō zhǒng wúxiàn chuánshū xiéyì, shēn shòu niánqīng yīnyuè àihàozhě de qīnglài. | This modular audio system not only delivers rich sound, but supports multiple wireless protocols, earning high praise from young music buffs. | Este equipo de sonido modular no sólo ofrece fidelidad acústica, sino conectividad inalámbrica, cautivando a los jóvenes melómanos.
  #2 | 大型建筑师团队将传统榫卯木构件与现代高强度碳纤维巧妙组合，打造出了具有东方美学的展馆顶棚。 | Dàxíng jiànzhùshī tuánduì jiāng chuántǒng sǔnmǎo mù gòujiàn yǔ xiàndài gāo qiángdù tànxiānwéi qiǎomiào zǔhé, dǎzào chū le jùyǒu dōngfāng měixué de zhǎnguǎn dǐngpéng. | Architects ingeniously combined traditional mortise-and-tenon timber with modern carbon fiber, crafting an exhibition canopy brimming with Oriental aesthetics. | Los arquitectos combinaron ensambles clásicos de madera con fibra de carbono, creando una cubierta que destila elegancia oriental.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  组合家具 | modular / sectional furniture
  强强组合 | combination of powerhouses
  音乐组合 | musical band / vocal group
  自由组合 | combine freely
  有机组合 | organic combination / integration
  重组 | restructure; reorganize

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  珠联璧合 | zhū lián bì hé | strings of pearls and linked jade; exquisite match of talents
  相得益彰 | xiāng dé yì zhāng | bring out the best in each other; mutual enhancement
  巧夺天工 | qiǎo duó tiān gōng | superb craftsmanship outdoing nature
  水乳交融 | shuǐ rǔ jiāo róng | blended like water and milk; deeply integrated

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  组 | zǔ | group; organize; braided silk cord | grupo; organizar; cordón de seda | 纟 | silk thread | 纟 (woven silk filaments) + 且 (ancestral altar / foundation) | 且 (qiě / phonetic association) | 8 | 左右结构 | Silk radical 纟 beside 且; braiding strands of silk together to form ornamental sashes or cords; organizing parts into teams. | Braiding separate strands of silk thread (纟) into a strong ceremonial cord (且): forming a group (组). | Trenzar hebras sueltas de seda (纟) en un cordel firme (且): formar un grupo o conjunto (组). | 214 | VFBM | 組
  合 | hé | join; close; fit together | unir; juntar; encajar | 人 | person | 人 (roof / covering lid) + 一 + 口 (box container) | 合 (hé) | 6 | 上下结构 | Lid 人 fitting over box 口; seamless convergence and closing together into a single whole. | Fitting a snug lid (人) onto a square box container (口) so they join seamlessly (合). | Ajustar una tapadera (人) sobre una caja (口) para que encajen a la perfección (合). | 35 | OMR | 合

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Braiding parts together like silk strands (组) and fitting them snugly (合) forms an assembled combination (组合).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Trenzar piezas sueltas (组) y ensamblarlas con ajuste perfecto (合) da lugar a una combinación sólida (组合).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Derived from classical silk weaving and joinery carpentry where composite structures gain strength exceeding single elements.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping third tone followed by rising second tone: 'zǔ hé' (214-35). Dip low on 'zǔ' and soar smoothly on 'hé'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    组 | zǔ | group; form | Silk radical 纟 with 且
